    "387": {
      "date": "2026-09-22",
      "edition": "Tuesday 22 September",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Miracle comeback",
          "heading": "France Women stun Australia with incredible second-half recovery in Aix-en-Provence",
          "body": "The France Women's rugby team secured a dramatic 29-26 victory against Australia on Saturday, overcoming both a 19-point deficit and a bizarre mid-match delay caused by a burning bus outside the Stade Maurice David. Despite a period of severe disciplinary trouble that saw the hosts reduced to 11 players, France clawed back momentum after half-time. Captain Pauline Bourdon Sansus helped steer the team to 17 unanswered points in the final 25 minutes to snatch an unlikely win."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Japan defeat Fiji to secure Pacific Nations Cup title",
