    "388": {
      "date": "2026-09-22",
      "edition": "Tuesday 22 September",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Tournament setback",
          "heading": "Ireland Women surrender 19-point lead in WXV defeat to United States",
          "body": "The Ireland Women's rugby team suffered a disappointing 40-36 defeat against the United States in their WXV Global Series opener at Tallaght Stadium. Despite building a commanding 31-12 lead early in the second half, Scott Bemand’s side succumbed to a late USA comeback as disciplinary issues and a numerical disadvantage took their toll. Bemand noted that the loss was \"a game we should have won,\" emphasising that his side must refine their technical process to maintain control for the full 80 minutes."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Japan defeat Fiji to secure Pacific Nations Cup title",
