      "edition": "Tuesday 22 September",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Azzurre victory",
          "heading": "Italy women dominate Japan with emphatic 55-21 WXV Global Series win",
          "body": "The Italy women's rugby team opened their WXV Global Series campaign with a comprehensive 55-21 victory over Japan at Stadio Omero Tognon. The Azzurre secured their largest-ever winning margin against the Sakura XV, highlighted by a prolific first-half burst that saw the hosts score three tries in seven minutes. Captain Vittoria Ostuni Minuzzi marked her 50th cap with a try, as Italy proved clinical in a match where they outplayed their opponents in all facets of the game."
        },
        {
