          "kicker": "WXV performance",
          "heading": "Wales Women deliver statement eight-try victory against South Africa in Cardiff",
          "body": "Wales Women set a new standard on Friday, producing an expansive display to dismantle South Africa 50-19 in their WXV Global Series opener. Coach Sean Lynn’s side, who had endured a nine-match winless streak, ran in eight tries as Sisilia Tuipulotu and player of the match Alex Callender starred. Lynn described the performance as the start of a “new DNA” for the team, built on improved skill development and a refreshed attacking intent ahead of their next test."
        },
